From 53c579cfe79a817acdeb9b5b9db3627b9641a9d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EscapeA <escapea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 04:15:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(chat): per-turn decode speed under the assistant message
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Show how fast the model decoded a turn: provider output tokens over the decode
wall time (first streamed chunk -> call end), the same quantity DeepSeek
Harness reports. Tool waits and first-token latency stay out of the ratio, and
a call without a recorded first chunk (non-streamed, failed stream, partial
stub) drops out instead of diluting it.

One reading per finished API call, pushed on usage.updated. The client hangs it
on the turn's latest assistant message, so the number stays readable after the
run ends — the run-scoped thinking indicator it would otherwise live in is
unmounted at that moment.

- bridge: forward first_chunk_at from the post_api_request hook
- chat-run: fold provider-timed calls into the run state
- client: render `N tok/s` under the turn's assistant message
